edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b44571e6-f5cf-5a50-a359-5da2ad7dfbff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311515 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186310336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311515 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311515 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311515 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186310336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311515 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f75ca1ce-9660-5f2b-8e80-e3b967d7673c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186310321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311526 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311526 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311526 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186310321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311526 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fa3b02da-876b-5e0a-8cf7-c53cb24cd812" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311737 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311737 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311737 #edb/ref 1069 "q-336699" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311737 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311737 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}},\\,Φ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n| ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $5{e}^{-t}$ |  | $\\,,\\,$ | ${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $-4$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186311737 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5ea97844-39dd-5c98-b9ff-e503c4be0f51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311737 #edb/ref 1074 "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{3t}-({e}^{3t})\\cdot 0}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{-4t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{-t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{-t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\int 5{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int -3{e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186311830 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186311052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311830 #edb/ref 1069 "q-337286" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311830 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311830 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}3t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\,\\,\\frac{1}{9}$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$23-15t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186311830 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fc7807df-c4d5-5658-9ef2-4f270abd2dc2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186311830 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & 3{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-3t}\\cdot 3{e}^{-t}-{e}^{-t}\\cdot {e}^{-3t}}\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2{e}^{-4t}}\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4t{e}^{3t} \\\\ -t{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\begin{bmatrix}4t{e}^{3t} \\\\ -t{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\int 4t{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int -t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=4t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=4\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4t{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(4t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\int \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}t{e}^{3t}-\\frac{4}{3}\\int {e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}t{e}^{3t}-\\frac{4}{9}{e}^{3t} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{e}^{3t}(3t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=-t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=-\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v={e}^{t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(-t)\\cdot {e}^{t}-\\int {e}^{t}(-\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-t{e}^{t}+\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-t{e}^{t}+{e}^{t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(1-t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & 3{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{9}{e}^{3t}(3t-1) \\\\ {e}^{t}(1-t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}4(3t-1)+9(1-t) \\\\ 4(3t-1)+27(1-t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}3t+5 \\\\ 23-15t\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186365599 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365599 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365599 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365599 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186365600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365599 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2b0824a7-3977-53c2-8ae9-fab24fac62a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365600 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365600 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365600 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eabf843f-76af-5374-87f3-015cd7c21177" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186482873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186482873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365601 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e2490d5f-d96a-5160-b6f7-a7d11c4a92d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365602 #edb/ref 1080 "-4{e}^{-4t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365602 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365602 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e7d357d-8554-535e-9625-2f454e5a740e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365793 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186496829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365793 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592